#include <stdio.h> - a preprocessor directive
to include the contents of the stdio.h library.
The brackets signify that the library is stored
in the standard library location (/usr/include
in this case).

int main (void) - a main function is an entry
point in every C program. Int specifies what
value will be returned and (void) specifies
what values (parameters) could be passed in.

puts("Test message"); - a function call; sta-
tement.

Statement - an instruction that describes a
single action. In C, they always end with a
semicolon - ;.

return 0; - exit status.

gcc - the GNU C Compiler.

echo $? - check the output of the last program ran.

C language is a statically typed language.

int(egers) - stores whole numbers; usually it's 32 bit
(4 bytes) wide or 2^32.
short int - is usually 16 bits wide (2 bytes).
long int - is usually 64 bits wide (8 bytes).
Unsigned int - uses the pos/neg bit to store
more positive values, effectively doubling
the pos values available.

char - stores characters, which are letters,
numbers, etc.; is 8 bits wide (1 byte).

Strings are not a separate type, but an array
of chars.

double - or double-precision floating point
number; is 64 bits wide (8 byte).

float - same as double, but less precise;
is 32 bits wide (4 bytes); must be suffixed
with f.

booleans - either true (1) or  false (0).

#include - one type of a preprocessor directive.
In this case, the preprocessor copies the contents
of the stated library into the source file.

Format specifiers:
1. %d, %i - int
2. %ld, %li - long int
3. %f - float
4. %lf, %g - double
5. %c - char
6. %s - string
7. %x - int, but hexadecimal

Full format specifier:
%[argument$][flags][width][.precision]type

Arguments example:
printf("%d * %d = %d", 4, 4, 16);
printf("%1$d * %1$d = %2$d", 4, 16);

RAM is usually split in 2 parts:
1. Stack - a space for short-lived that
operates on a FILO model.
2. Heap - a space for long-lived, larger data.

sizeof - evaluate the size of an object or type.

static - when a static variable goes out of the 
scope, it retains it's value.
